tart: restart app? Let's force stop and reopen? open_app brings to foreground, doesn't reset data. Maybe kill app via app switch swipe? Hmm, we can't force stop easily. But perhaps the setting persists; toggling \"Hidden Files\" might turn it on. But dialog empty.\n\nAlternative: the initial 28 count might be stale/incorrect from some previous state and not important.\n\nB. Drawer storage list resolved each open: test open drawer repeatedly. Should show Internal Storage. Maybe a bug: after opening drawer second time, storage list shows duplicated entries or free space stale after copying a big file. Let's test by opening drawer multiple times.\n\nC. Multi-file overflow toggle: tested works. But maybe there's a bug with the toggle when all items are selected but then deselect one: label should become \"Select All\". Test. Also check the label after rotating (we saw in landscape action toolbar has a separate \"Select All\" button rather than overflow). Hmm.\n\nD. Properties: test folder with nested large content (e.g., root or Android) to see background computation. Maybe the bug: size shows only direct items? Let's test Android folder (huge - would take long). Maybe \"Documents\" folder. The background task might update the size but date remains stale? Let's test a folder with multiple items: root folder properties maybe enormous (452 GB?) Actually Android folder size big. We have time.\n\nFirst, let's close this dialog (CLOSE)."}
