{"type": "thinking", "text": "Tapping Internal Storage closed drawer, stayed at root. Fine.\n\nNow check drawer folder shortcuts: DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures with edit icons. These are likely \"quick access\" / bookmarks? But precondition says no bookmarks added. Hmm, these might be default shortcuts computed from... Wait these entries in drawer under Internal Storage, before categories, are \"bookmarks\"? In Amaze, the drawer shows \"Quick access\" (bookmarks) as a list of folders — normally empty with \"No bookmarks\". Then category views. Here it shows DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures, each with a pencil (edit) icon. Precondition says \"No bookmarks have been added.\" So if drawer shows pre-existing bookmarks, that contradicts preconditions! Hmm, but maybe these are default \"storage volumes' folders\"? Actually Amaze's drawer has \"Quick access\" section listing bookmarked folders. Default bookmarks in Amaze include? I believe Amaze's default bookmarks are empty initially. But some builds have default \"Pictures\", \"Movies\", etc.? Hmm.\n\nWait: actually the drawer's top section under Internal Storage are \"quick access\" items = bookmarks. In Amaze 3.11, fresh install may have default bookmarks? I don't think so. But precondition explicitly says no bookmarks added — maybe to test adding bookmark via \"Add to Bookmarks\" and then checking drawer. We saw context menu \"Add to Bookmarks\" for folders. If there are already 5 bookmarks, that's a precondition violation. But maybe those entries are not bookmarks but default \"library folders\" (like standard directories) shown by Amaze. In Amaze 3.11 the drawer does have a section of \"Quick access\" with default entries? Let me recall: Amaze screenshot: drawer shows \"Internal Storage\" then folders like \"Android\", \"DCIM\", \"Download\", \"Movies\", \"Music\", \"Pictures\", then \"Quick access\" (star icon) ... Actually the default bookmarks in Amaze ARE Android, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. Yes! I recall Amaze has default bookmarks pointing to these folders. Hmm, in that case precondition \"No bookmarks have been added\" might mean none added by tester, defaults exist.\n\nThe drawer shows DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures (missing Android? maybe hidden due to scroll/overlap). Fine.\n\nLet's test adding a bookmark to AndroidQA/Amaze and see it appear in drawer, then remove it? There's \"Add to Bookmarks\" in folder context. But \"no bookmarks have been added\" suggests we may add one to test. Hmm, but we should not modify data more than needed; bookmarks are app state, can remove? There might not be a remove option except edit (pencil) to remove. This is part of navigation drawer area likely. But the changed list doesn't mention bookmarks. Still, \"navigation drawer\" as a whole.\n\nLet's prioritize bugs indicated by changed notes. The changed notes are hints at what was changed, and bugs likely introduced there:\n1. Category views: file list on-screen controls switch entering/leaving. Bug could be that controls don't switch correctly (e.g., FAB or sort buttons remain/wrong).\n2. Multi-file overflow: bulk-marking entry toggle. Bug could be label/state mismatch.\n3. Drawer storage list: volumes resolved each time drawer opens. Bug could be volumes list not refreshing / duplicated / crash.\n4. Properties: folder size/date background task after dialog opens. Bug could be stale values or wrong date or updated too late / not updated.\n\nLet me test each more aggressively.\n\nCategory views: enter each category (Quick access, Recent files, Images, Videos, Audio, Documents, APKs) and check on-screen controls. In portrait, the top bar normally has Search, Home, More. In landscape it had Sort and History buttons. In category maybe the toolbar should show sort/history? The \"on-screen controls\" likely refers to the FAB and multi-select etc. Let me enter Videos, Audio, Documents, APKs, Quick access, Recent files and observe differences. Note, root categories show all matching files across storage. Videos/Audio empty. Documents category maybe shows? Let's test.\n\nOpen drawer -> tap Videos."}
