{"type": "thinking", "text": "Rotation dismissed the properties dialog entirely. Is that expected? Hmm. The properties dialog is lost on rotation. Many dialogs survive config change. This might be a bug, but the changed note says \"folder sizes and dates are now computed in the background by a separate task after the dialog opens\". If dialog is dismissed on rotate, the background task may update a destroyed view — no visible issue. Hmm.\n\nNot sure whether rotation dialog dismissal is standard Amaze behavior (it might be a DialogFragment that should survive). We should note it but is it in scope? \"File properties dialog\" area. Device rotation check says nothing lost. Losing the properties dialog on rotation could be a bug. But might be normal for this app.\n\nHmm, but I shouldn't over-report. Let me focus on the likely injected bugs.\n\nLet's dig into the properties background-computation behavior: maybe the bug is that the size/date are never updated for folders whose computation takes longer (large folders). E.g., root folder properties would be huge; the dialog might show \"0 items; 0 B\" or \"-\" and never update. Test with a folder with many files: e.g., root has 14 folders, or \"Android\" huge. If the background task is broken, size would remain 0 or \"Calculating...\". For Alpha and Beta it computed 13/12 B quickly. For Amaze 41.05 kB. All good. Maybe the bug involves dates: folder date might be updated to now after background (incorrect date). We saw Nov 14 7:30 for Alpha/Beta/Amaze, which matches. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the injected properties bug is a stale-value issue: when you open properties of folder A, close, then open properties of folder B, you briefly see A's size? We opened Alpha then Beta then Amaze. In Beta dialog we saw \"1 item; 12 B\" immediately — correct. Amaze correct.\n\nWhat about the \"Date\" for folders: is it Last Modified? Alpha's readme date Nov 14 7:30. Fine.\n\nMaybe the background computation updates the dialog even after it's closed, and when you open a different folder's properties quickly, the old async result overwrites the new dialog values. This is a classic bug: \"folder sizes and dates are now computed in the background by a separate task after the dialog opens\" — if the task isn't canceled/checked when dialog changes, values from the previous folder can appear. Test: Open properties of a big folder (e.g., Android), close immediately, then open properties of Alpha quickly, see if Alpha shows Android's huge size. Or open Alpha properties then quickly close and open Beta — check whether Beta shows Alpha's 13 B vs 12 B. We saw Beta correct, but timing may not hit.\n\nSimilarly, the async task might be attached to an Activity and when you open the same dialog again, the old result applies. Let's test rapid sequence. Need to be careful; opening from menu takes taps.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the bug is that folder size text initially shows \"0 items; 0 B\" then updates after a delay. That's expected (\"computed in the background after the dialog opens\"). But if the dialog updates *after* it's closed and reopened for another folder, bug.\n\nLet's test: open properties of Beta (12 B), close, immediately open Alpha (13 B) and check. Already did (Alpha then Beta) and both correct.\n\nMaybe test a large folder where computation takes time. Open root? We can't get properties of root easily; but Android folder (huge). Let's do Android properties and observe initial and after waiting. If it stays \"0 items; 0 B\" or \"Calculating...\" that's a bug.\n\nLet me go to root and open Android properties. Currently landscape. Rotate back portrait first."}
