create a big file via terminal command, but that's outside typical QA data changes. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the storage list bug: the drawer's \"Internal Storage\" row has an edit icon (pencil) and clicking it opens a \"rename/remove\" dialog? Actually the pencil icons next to folder shortcuts are for editing bookmarks. The Internal Storage row has a zigzag graph icon on right (storage usage). Hmm.\n\nMaybe the \"storage volumes resolved each time drawer opens\" bug relates to SD card detection. Only internal storage here, so hard to detect a bug unless duplicates appear.\n\nWait — perhaps the drawer shows \"Internal Storage 369 GB free of 452 GB\" but correct free space should be different? We can check system storage settings? Hard.\n\nHmm. Let's think about the multi-file toggle more. Changed: \"the bulk-marking entry is now handled as an on/off toggle of the current state.\" Possible intended behavior: the overflow menu entry should be \"Select All\" when not all selected, and \"Deselect All\" when all selected. We verified. But what about when some selected and you tap \"Select All\": it selected all 6, good. What about when 0 selected? Action mode can't have 0 normally, except after rotation bug. In our rotated state, action mode had 0 selected and toolbar shown \"Select All\" button (landscape) — tapping that would select all. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug: when all items selected, \"Deselect All\" appears, but pressing it deselects all AND exits action mode. That's fine.\n\nCould there be a bug where after tapping \"Select All\", the *label* on the action bar count doesn't update? It updated to 6.\n\nMaybe the toggle should be \"Invert selection\" in some versions? No.\n\nLet's inspect what happens when folder contains files AND folders: Select All selects both (6). Good. \"Share\" shown with 2 selected? In Amaze, share multiple is allowed? Hmm, the menu with 2 selected showed Share, Compress, Hide, Select All but no \"Open with\"/\"Add Shortcut\". Perhaps expected.\n\nNow to find the injected bug in multi-file menu, try entering multi-select via long-press, select all, then tap \"Deselect All\" then reopen menu and see if \"Select All\" is shown (it should). But after deselect all action mode exits; long-press again shows subset.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug occurs in a category view (Images) where select-all selects only visible files? Eh.\n\nLet's test multi-select in Images category view: long-press photo, select all (2), toggle. Then maybe share. Also check that action mode count and controls work in category view. The \"on-screen controls switching\" might affect multi-select; e.g., in category view the selection action bar might have wrong buttons. Let's test.\n\nNavigate to Images category. Currently in Android/data/com.amaze.filemanager. Use drawer. Open drawer (element 0)."}
