{"type": "thinking", "text": "Works: tap storage row returns to root.\n\nNote the folder shortcut entries \"DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures\" with pencil icons are bookmarks? Precondition says no bookmarks. But these default bookmarks maybe injected? Hmm. Let's test bookmark behavior to see if these are indeed bookmarks: long-press/click pencil on DCIM in drawer -> probably opens \"Edit bookmark\" dialog. If precondition says no bookmarks, maybe these are \"quick access\" defaults expected. I'll not report.\n\nNow, let's look for the hidden files reset bug more. The count went 28 -> 14 after entering category Images and leaving. That is a real inconsistency: the file list control \"Show hidden files\" state changed. To reproduce from current, I need to turn hidden files on again. The menu item \"Hidden Files\" dialog is empty. Maybe tapping \"Hidden Files\" actually toggles the setting (the dialog is just a confirmation?). Let's test: currently 14 folders. Tap overflow -> Hidden Files -> then close, see if count becomes 28. Earlier I did that at 14 and it remained 14. So no.\n\nHmm, so how did it go from 28 to 14? Wait, maybe initial 28 was not hidden files but the count included the files? Initial: \"28 folders and 0 files\". If hidden files were shown, 28 folders. Now 14. Maybe the difference is that initial view was \"Home\" showing all folders including hidden (because \"Show hidden files\" setting initially on). Then I tapped \"Hidden Files\" menu which toggled it off (despite showing an empty dialog). Actually sequence: initial 28 (hidden on). I tapped overflow > \"Hidden Files\" -> dialog empty, tapped CLOSE. Then count became 14 when I returned from Images. Wait, but the count 14 was observed after entering Images and backing out, which happened BEFORE I first tapped Hidden Files. Let me re-check chronology:\n\n1. Start: 28 folders.\n2. Open drawer, tap Images. Images 2 files.\n3. More options -> same menu; back.\n4. Tap \"Navigate up\" (hamburger) -> drawer; tap outside.\n5. Press BACK -> root: \"14 folders and 0 files\". ← So count changed before any Hidden Files tap!\n\nSo entering Images and leaving changed 28 -> 14. No hidden files tap involved. So the category view reset the hidden files filter. That's a solid bug for the category view area! The changed note says entering/leaving category views switches on-screen controls; maybe the implementation resets something, causing hidden files to be hidden. The visible manifestation: root folder count changes from \"28 folders and 0 files\" to \"14 folders and 0 files\" and hidden folders (.trashed etc.) disappear after visiting a category view. That's a state inconsistency.\n\nTo report confidently, I need to reproduce: start with hidden files shown (28). How to get back to 28? The Hidden Files menu dialog may have a toggle not visible? Since it's empty, maybe tapping the dialog area toggles? Hmm.\n\nMaybe the app's hidden files setting is stored and toggled by a menu item with a checkmark. Wait, the menu item \"Hidden Files\" opened a dialog, but maybe the dialog is actually a *sort* or *filter* dialog with a list of options that failed to render (empty). The state change from 28 to 14 wasn't due to opening that dialog though.\n\nCould the initial 28 be because the app was launched in a state where hidden files were shown, and entering category view (\"Images\") uses a different loader that sets \"showHidden=false\" globally? Plausible implementation bug: category view's onResume applies its own filter to the main list's shared preference. Or the \"on-screen controls\" switch resets hidden files.\n\nTo reproduce reliably, maybe rotate? or restart app? If we restart the app (force stop), the app may start with hidden files on again? The setting might persist as off now. Hmm.\n\nWe can force-stop the app via recents (swipe away may not stop). Or use Settings? Not accessible maybe. We could use the app's \"Exit\" menu which likely exits and maybe resets? That might restore initial state? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, use \"Open in Terminal\" to run commands, but that won't change app setting.\n\nActually, maybe the hidden files setting is toggled via long-press the \"Hidden Files\" menu item? In Amaze, menu items with checkboxes show a checkmark; maybe \"Hidden Files\" opens a dialog listing hidden files? Let me search memory: Amaze v3.11.3 might have a \"Hidden Files\" dialog with a single CheckBox \"Show hidden files\" and positive button \"OK\". If the checkbox is not showing (empty body), tapping the body area might toggle it. The dialog's body is blank but there could be an invisible checkbox at the top-left of the body. We could tap around y=1100 maybe. But this is a bug itself (invisible checkbox). Not our scope though.\n\nAlternatively, maybe 28 folders initially because the app was showing all folders including hidden due to a \"show hidden\" default at first launch; then the state got persisted off. Maybe the app was freshly launched with default \"show hidden on\" but our first visit to category changed it. Hard to re-enable.\n\nCould reproduce the reverse direction: maybe entering category also changes the *sort* setting, etc. The count change is enough evidence with the observation quote \"28 folders and 0 files\" vs \"14 folders and 0 files\". But is it a bug or expected? Hidden files disappearing after visiting an image category and returning seems clearly a bug. However, the instruction says reproduce once before reporting. I observed once. We should attempt reproduction even if we can't easily restore hidden files. Could we make hidden files appear again by restarting app? Let's try killing the app via Recents (app switch, swipe away). Then open_app. If hidden files setting default resets on launch, we'd get 28 again and can reproduce.\n\nLet's do that. Press APP_SWITCH, swipe away Amaze, then open_app."}
