{"type": "thinking", "text": "Quick access shows 0/0 and No Files. But wait, precondition says \"No bookmarks have been added\", so Quick access empty. But the drawer shows folder shortcuts DCIM etc. — if those were bookmarks, Quick access wouldn't be empty. So those are NOT bookmarks; they're something else (maybe devices' \"shortcut folders\"). Good, precondition holds.\n\nSo Quick access empty is correct.\n\nNow Documents view: AndroidQA/Amaze has notes.txt and report+final.txt .txt; are .txt considered documents? Let's check. Also maybe property/count. Not critical.\n\nLet's test the \"Set As Home\" in category view as it's an on-screen control that may be wrong. In category view (Quick access), overflow -> Set As Home. If selected, app's home becomes Quick access. Then tapping Home button returns to Quick access; and maybe the \"Home\" path label \"Quick access\". Is that intended? Probably not but plausible feature. It could break. Since changed note says controls switch, maybe \"Set As Home\" should be hidden in category views. Hmm.\n\nBetter approach: compare to how the app likely should behave. Let's check the overflow menu in category view vs folder view. Earlier both showed the same seven items: Sort, History, Grid View, Hidden Files, Set As Home, Open in Terminal, Exit. In category view, \"Set As Home\" may make little sense but not necessarily a bug.\n\nLet's test leaving category via Home button and via drawer: both should restore normal controls. We did via BACK. FAB restored. What if you leave a category by tapping a storage folder bookmark (DCIM) or the Internal Storage row? Then also leave; test controls. E.g., enter Images, then open drawer and tap Internal Storage; check FAB restored. Likely fine.\n\nWhat about entering a category from a non-root folder then leaving: does it return to the previous folder or root? Earlier we entered Images from root. Let's test from Amaze folder: navigate to AndroidQA/Amaze, open drawer, tap Images, then BACK. Does it go back to Amaze or root? In Amaze, category view is a \"virtual\" view; back likely returns to previous folder. Let's test; this is state/navigation consistency.\n\nLet's do: Back from Quick access to root. Navigate AndroidQA/Amaze. Open drawer, Images, then BACK. Observe."}
