tale result isn't visible. Could open properties of the root Android folder (0 B) then quickly switch to Amaze (41 kB). If the background task from the previous dialog completes late, it might overwrite Amaze's size with 0 B or vice versa. But small/tiny times.\n\nMaybe use \"Android\" folder whose scan may take a bit longer (3 items with SAF restricted subfolder), then open Alpha quickly. Steps: from root, tap Android properties -> opens; immediately tap OK; navigate AndroidQA/Amaze; open Beta properties. That's many taps; async likely done.\n\nI think the properties feature is fine. Maybe the seeded bug there is rotation dismisses dialog, which is a visible state loss. Actually a DialogFragment with background task: rotation would dismiss/recreate. If the dialog isn't a DialogFragment but plain AlertDialog created in Activity, rotation dismisses it; that's common but considered acceptable? The test instruction explicitly says \"Device: rotate the screen, and check that nothing is lost.\" So we can report that rotating closes the properties dialog. But is that a real bug? Many Android apps lose dialogs on rotation, but good ones preserve. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe while properties dialog is open, the background task updates the *wrong dialog* after rotation. E.g., rotate while properties for Alpha open; dialog disappears; then the async task tries to update and crashes? We rotated with Amaze dialog open and nothing crashed. Fine.\n\nLet me look for more concrete bugs in properties. Consider the \"Hide from media browsers\" checkbox; when tapped, does it require OK to apply? The dialog only has \"OK\" (no Cancel). For files, there's no checkbox, only OK. Fine.\n\nMaybe the folder properties \"Size\" should compute in background and show \"Calculating...\" but instead shows a wrong \"0 B\" for Android (maybe correct). Could test a folder that definitely has files, like root /storage/emulated/0 (properties of the current directory). We can't open properties of current folder, but we can open properties of DCIM? probably empty. What about Android/media? Let's check /storage/emulated/0/Android/media maybe contains stuff (alarms/notifications/ringtones?). Actually media folder may hold audio; likely empty.\n\nCould test /storage/emulated/0/Movies maybe empty; DCIM maybe empty.\n\nThe only folders with files are Amaze (41 kB) and Alpha/Beta. We tested all. Sizes correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the date bug: For Beta (12 B) and Alpha (13 B) properties show date Nov 14 7:30—matches list. For Amaze 7:30—matches list. Good.\n\nCould test that folder properties' Size updates after adding a file while dialog is open? We could use the app to copy a file while dialog open? Can't interact with list behind dialog.\n\nMaybe open properties of a folder, then tap \"OK\", then immediately reopen—should be same. Fine.\n\nMaybe the injected bug is that the \"Date\" for folders is computed in background and *always displays today's date/time* (e.g., \"Nov 14 | 7:38 AM\") rather than the folder's mtime. But we saw Alpha 7:36 vs Beta 7:30; different, matching. So no.\n\nMaybe the date format for folders is wrong (e.g., no time) - no.\n\nLet's test properties on a file to ensure size and date correct, and MD5/SHA-256 stable across reopen. We saw notes 15 B MD5 ade1... Let's reopen and compare hash. Could hash be computed in background and show empty initially? It showed immediately. Reopen to see same hash. Quick. Current in Amaze folder. Tap notes.txt properties (20), then Properties."}
