ight-side graph icon? Element 43 imageButton next to Internal Storage in drawer. Maybe that opens a storage usage screen. Not needed.\n\nLet me test the drawer storage row when in category view and after rotation.\n\nActually, a stronger approach: use \"History\" to see recent locations? no.\n\nMaybe the drawer bug is this: We noticed the initial drawer screenshot showed folder shortcuts DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures with pencil edit icons. After we navigated to Amaze and opened drawer, the accessibility labels included \"Alpha\", \"Beta\", \"notes.txt\" etc., but visually the drawer still showed the same 5. So accessibility merging only. Fine.\n\nCould the drawer storage list be missing the \"free of total\" after the first open? Always present.\n\nMaybe the storage list is resolved asynchronously and initially empty on the very first drawer open after launch. At our first open, it was populated. Fine.\n\nWhat if the drawer is opened while the device is rotated to landscape? It shows Internal Storage. Fine.\n\nWhat if storage row is tapped twice? We did; navigates home. Fine.\n\nI'm starting to think the drawer change has no seeded bug or is hard to trigger.\n\nLet's revisit category views for more bugs. Enter each category and compare counts:\n- Images: 0 folders and 2 files (correct).\n- Videos: 0/0 no files (correct).\n- Audio: likely 0/0 (correct).\n- Documents: should list .txt files? Let's check. Files in AndroidQA/Amaze: notes.txt, report+final.txt, plus readme.txt x2. Documents category may only show document mime types (.txt). It might show 4 files. Let's test count. If it shows 0/0 but lists files, that's same count bug.\n- APKs: likely 0.\n- Recent files: 0/0 but 6 files (bug).\n- Quick access: 0/0 empty (correct).\n\nLet's check Documents and Audio."}
