{"type": "thinking", "text": "Quick access still shows \"No Files\" despite a bookmark \"Amaze\" existing. So either Quick access isn't bookmarks, or it's broken. Hmm.\n\nLet's check the bookmark appears in drawer: yes. So \"Quick access\" is likely a different feature. In Amaze, \"Quick access\" might be \"recently accessed folders\" or maybe a \"quick access\" list of shortcuts (bookmarks). If it's the latter, it's a bug that the newly added Amaze bookmark doesn't show. But the empty state \"No Files\" (not \"No bookmarks\" or \"No folders\") suggests it's a file listing category, maybe \"Quick access\" = files tagged as favorites? Hmm.\n\nLet me search memory: Amaze File Manager has in drawer: \"Quick access\" (maybe shows 3 most recently used folders?), \"Recent files\", \"Images\", \"Videos\", \"Audio\", \"Documents\", \"APKs\". Hmm, \"Quick access\" is likely the \"Bookmarks\" view (star icon). The default drawer bookmarks (DCIM etc.) might be *suggested shortcuts* from storage volumes, not actual bookmarks. When I added Amaze bookmark, it appeared in drawer *and* should appear in Quick access. It didn't. That would be a bug in the navigation drawer category views. But is this in scope of the changed note? Category views yes.\n\nHmm wait, maybe Quick access is empty because the app's bookmark list view only shows *files*? No, bookmarks are folders. Quick access should show folders. The header \"0 folders and 0 files\" + \"No Files\" is suspicious. It might be that the Quick access view is failing to load the bookmark list. This could be a seeded bug for the category views change: \"the file list now switches its on-screen controls when entering and leaving these views\" — not about content. But maybe.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Quick access shows *recently opened files* (like history) but it's empty because no file opened yet. We haven't opened any file. The \"Recent files\" view lists 6 files because they were created recently? Hmm, recent files are from media store/history? It listed all 6 files in Amaze, suggesting \"Recent files\" uses recent documents provider or file last-modified. Quick access empty maybe because nothing bookmarked? But we bookmarked Amaze.\n\nLet me test after adding bookmark: reopen drawer to confirm bookmark still there, then maybe Quick access updates. It showed No Files after adding. Still No Files.\n\nMaybe \"Quick access\" is for \"frequently accessed folders\" computed from history. Since we navigated around a lot, you'd expect some. Hmm.\n\nI'm not sure. Let's look at the Quick access icon: star. In Amaze, the bookmarks feature's icon is a star. The drawer item \"Add to Bookmarks\" confirms bookmarks exist. The Quick access drawer item is likely the bookmarks screen. So a bookmarked folder should appear there. It doesn't. That's a functional bug: bookmarked folder doesn't appear in Quick access. But the test area \"navigation drawer\" includes storage list, not bookmarks. Changed in build doesn't mention bookmarks. It could be a distraction.\n\nWait, maybe the star \"Quick access\" is a *folder* named Quick access? No, path shows \"Quick access\" as fullpath (a virtual path). It's a category.\n\nLet me check Amaze docs from memory: Drawer sections: \"Quick access\" (bookmarks) is a heading, under which bookmarked folders are listed (DCIM, Download...). The star icon \"Quick access\" entry might toggle/collapse? Hmm. Actually in the screenshot, the five folders (DCIM etc.) appear in a block *above* the divider, then below the divider there are entries with icons: star \"Quick access\", clock \"Recent files\", image \"Images\", video \"Videos\", music \"Audio\", document \"Documents\", apk \"APKs\". These latter are \"special views\". The block above the divider is likely \"Quick access\" bookmarks (since they're quick-access folders), and the star entry \"Quick access\" is a view of *all* quick access items including files? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the block above the divider may be \"storage shortcuts\" auto-generated for standard folders; the star \"Quick access\" view shows bookmarks. Then Amaze bookmark should appear in Quick access, but doesn't. Hmm.\n\nActually, I recall Amaze drawer structure: Under each storage volume, it lists \"bookmarks\" (quick access) for that volume. The star \"Quick access\" item opens a screen listing all bookmarks. So yes, it should list Amaze. Since it doesn't, potential bug.\n\nBut wait, did the \"Add to Bookmarks\" actually persist? The drawer showed \"Amaze\" folder with pencil icon at top, above DCIM. That indicates the bookmark was added. So the Quick access category should show it. It shows No Files. That's a real inconsistency.\n\nLet me verify more: Is there another way to see bookmarks? In the drawer, the quick-access block shows Amaze. So bookmark exists. Quick access view empty = bug. This is within \"navigation drawer\" area (quick access is a drawer category view). Hmm, but the changed note is specifically \"Navigation drawer category views: the file list now switches its on-screen controls when entering and leaving these views.\" Not content. Still, a bug is a bug.\n\nLet me also check the Quick access screen's controls: no FAB (category view). Fine.\n\nBefore reporting, let's see whether Quick access maybe only shows bookmarks when \"show hidden\" etc. Or maybe it lists bookmarks of *files* not folders? In Amaze, you can bookmark files too? \"Add to Bookmarks\" appears in folder context menu only? For files, maybe also. Bookmarks can be files or folders. Quick access likely shows both. It shows 0 folders/0 files.\n\nLet's try adding a *file* to bookmarks (notes.txt) and see if Quick access shows it. If Quick access is for files, it might show the file. But if it still shows nothing, bug confirmed. Let's test with notes.txt bookmark, then remove both bookmarks.\n\nActually removing bookmarks: In the drawer, the pencil icon next to Amaze likely opens an edit dialog with delete. Let's figure out removal later.\n\nAdd notes.txt to bookmarks: navigate Amaze, tap three-dot notes, \"Add to Bookmarks\". We saw file context menu earlier had no \"Add to Bookmarks\" (it had Open with, Cut, Copy, Delete, Rename, Encrypt, Properties, Compress, Share). So only folders can be bookmarked. Quick access should show folders.\n\nLet's verify Quick access once more after reopening drawer: open drawer now, tap Quick access again. Already did. Still empty.\n\nHmm, the \"Quick access\" view might only show *frequently used* items, not bookmarks. But the star icon = bookmarks in Amaze. I'd like stronger evidence. Could check Amaze docs? Can't access internet. Could inspect app strings? Can't read code.\n\nLet's think about the name: In the drawer, above the divider, the default entries are DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. These are likely the \"quick access\" bookmarks. The star entry below is also labeled \"Quick access\", suggesting the drawer section header isn't shown (maybe hidden). Actually maybe the star \"Quick access\" entry, when tapped, shows the *bookmarks* view - which should show those same folders. Empty is clearly inconsistent.\n\nI think this is worth a report, but the developer may reject as out of scope/by design. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe there is a delay: Quick access loads bookmarks asynchronously and we observed immediately. Let's wait a bit."}
