 ?\n   - drawer another category: switches (no restore).\n   The seeded bug might be that the FAB state is wrong for *some* routes. We found Home. Maybe also after leaving via drawer storage row the FAB missing. Test:\n     Enter Images -> open drawer -> tap Internal Storage -> check FAB. Could be missing too. If so, that strengthens the report (multi-route). But the developer already confirmed the Home route. Fine.\n\n2. Multi-file overflow menu: \"bulk-marking entry is now handled as an on/off toggle of the current state.\" Maybe the seeded bug is that tapping the toggle *when some items are selected* only selects the remaining? Or tapping \"Select All\" selects *the visible items only* (pagination)? The list has pagination: at root 14 folders with 2 pages; in Amaze 6 items might fit on one page? We saw 6 items all selected. What if a folder has more than one page of items? Then Select All might select only current page. But not enough items here. Amaze has 6 (fits). Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug is that \"Select All\" in the *category view* selects all files across all folders? It selected 2 images. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug: after tapping \"Select All\" (all 6), the overflow menu now shows \"Deselect All\"; but if you then tap \"Deselect All\", the action bar exits and count 0. That's fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is that \"Deselect All\" deselects but leaves *one* item selected? We tested: exited cleanly with 0 selected and FAB back. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is with the toggle *when the menu is opened via long-press on an already selected item*? Hmm.\n\nWhat about selecting all with the *action bar \"Select All\" in landscape*: works.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the menu item label is correct but the *icon/checkmark* state is wrong. The observe doesn't show checkmarks. Hard.\n\n3. Drawer storage list: \"volumes resolved each time drawer opens.\" Maybe the seeded bug is that opening the drawer while in a **category view** causes the storage volumes to be resolved to the category's pseudo-storage, or the drawer shows *no* storage row, or shows duplicate storage rows. Let's test opening drawer in each category and compare. We did enter Images etc. but didn't inspect drawer in category view. Let's test: enter Images, open drawer, observe storage row. Maybe there's a duplicate or wrong label. Also in Videos/Audio/APKs/Recent/Quick access. Let's check.\n\n4. Properties: \"folder sizes and dates computed in background by separate task after dialog opens.\" Maybe the bug appears when opening properties of a folder and then rotating while background task pending: the dialog is dismissed (we observed) — maybe that's the intended bug: the dialog should stay open on rotation, or the background task crashes. Or maybe the bug is that the *date* value is wrong for folders (e.g., always shows today's date). We saw dates matching. Or the size is computed only for direct children not recursive—Amaze nested test showed recursive inclusion (13+12 inside subfolders). Hmm.\n\nLet's test properties of a folder with many nested levels and a *large* size to see if the background update causes a visible change and if it matches. We only have small data. Could create a bigger nested structure via copy: copy the 4 files into Alpha many times? That changes data but can be cleaned. Or easier: the \"AndroidQA\" folder contains Amaze (41.05 kB) + nothing else. Properties should show \"1 item; 41.05 kB\". Let's verify to test recursion. We'll do later.\n\nMaybe the properties bug is about *empty folders showing \"items; 0 B\"* which we found. Developer said can't reproduce, but maybe our report steps were misread. Could refile with clue \"size line starts with 'items;'\" and mention both Alarms and Audiobooks. Actually the developer may have tested a non-empty folder because they didn't read that the folder must be empty. Our report said \"empty folder\". Hmm.\n\nLet me inspect the exact rendering of an empty folder properties again after a fresh restart (maybe the count now shows 0). Currently root with 14. Open Alarms properties and observe carefully, maybe waiting. Let's do quickly."}
