(new bookmarks lost on restart), because the drawer storage list change might have affected bookmark storage. Hmm, unlikely.\n\nCould the bookmark loss be because the app *crashed* from LeakCanary memory dump before saving? No, SharedPreferences are saved immediately.\n\nLet's test bookmark persistence again cleanly: Add Amaze bookmark, verify drawer, then just rotate (not restart) and see if it's still there. If it vanishes on rotation/drawer reopen, that might be the \"storage volumes resolved each time the drawer opens\" bug: the drawer rebuild resets the bookmark list to defaults, dropping newly added bookmarks! That would fit! The change re-resolves storage volumes each drawer open, and maybe it inadvertently resets bookmarks/shortcuts. Let's test:\n\n1. Add Amaze bookmark.\n2. Open drawer -> see Amaze.\n3. Close drawer, reopen -> is Amaze still there? Earlier when we added Amaze, it appeared; after restart it vanished. But maybe it vanished immediately on the next drawer open, and we didn't check before exit. Let's test now.\n\nWe'll do: navigate AndroidQA, add Amaze bookmark (already added once but lost; add again), open drawer, close, reopen, check. If it disappears on reopen, that's the seeded bug! Great idea.\n\nCurrent state: properties dialog for AndroidQA open. Close (10). Then we need to add Amaze bookmark: at root now, tap AndroidQA (14), then 3-dot on Amaze (10), Add to Bookmarks. Then open drawer (0), observe bookmarks, close, reopen, observe. Let's do."}
