{"type": "thinking", "text": "Correctly shows \"Select All\" after deselecting one. The toggle state recalculates. Good. Then tap Select All (0) to select all again; should show 6, then reopen to Deselect All. That's repetition. Works earlier. Let's skip.\n\nHmm. What about selecting all via toggle, then deselecting one by *toggling \"Deselect All\"*? That exits. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is that when the \"Selection\" is not all and you tap \"Select All\", the share/open-with entries disappear but that's expected for multiple items.\n\nMulti-file area maybe tests file operations: copy, cut, delete, compress, share, rename, properties for multiple files. We tested copy+delete. Could test \"Compress\" multiple files -> creates zip, then delete zip. That's more data changes. Could find a bug where the zip isn't created or named wrong. But not indicated by changed note.\n\nLet's re-read the changed notes carefully:\n\n- Navigation drawer category views: the file list now switches its on-screen controls when entering and leaving these views.\n- Multi-file overflow menu: the bulk-marking entry is now handled as an on/off toggle of the current state.\n- Navigation drawer storage list: the storage volumes are now resolved each time the drawer opens.\n- File properties dialog: folder sizes and dates are now computed in the background by a separate task after the dialog opens.\n\nThese are likely descriptions of correct behavior of new features, each possibly with a seeded bug. We found the first. For the others, maybe the bugs are subtle and our tests passed because we didn't do the exact right thing. Let's hypothesize each:\n\nMulti-file overflow toggle: The intended behavior \"handled as an on/off toggle of the current state\" means the menu entry should show \"Select All\" when not all selected, \"Deselect All\" when all selected. We verified. Maybe the seeded bug is that it *only* toggles the *visible page* items, not all items in the folder. In a folder with multiple pages, Select All might select only the current page. Our Amaze folder has 6 items on one page (all visible) - no bug triggered. The root folder has 14 folders (2 pages) - if we enter multi-select at root and tap Select All, does it select all 14 (count 14) or only the visible 9? Let's test! This could be the seeded bug: bulk marking only selects the current page instead of all items. The count after Select All would show e.g., 9 instead of 14. That's a strong candidate and easy to test.\n\nLet's go to root (Home), long-press a folder, open overflow, tap Select All, see count. Expected 14; if it shows 9 (page size), bug. Let's test. First exit current action mode (Done 26), then Home (3). Then long-press Alarms, overflow, Select All, observe count. Do it."}
