{"type": "thinking", "text": "Deselect All exits properly. Multi-file toggle seems robust.\n\nMaybe the seeded multi-file bug is about the overflow menu being an *on/off toggle* while the entry label should also be updated in the *landscape toolbar button*; we saw it toggles. Fine.\n\nCould there be a bug where \"Select All\" is shown even when all items are selected (label not toggling) in a *different context*, e.g., when the menu is opened while scroll position is on page 2? Hmm. We opened after all selected in portrait at page 1; label was Deselect All. What if the all-selected state is on page 2? The label should still be Deselect All. Our 14 selection included page 2; we opened menu while at page 1. Could test scrolled to page 2 with all selected -> open menu -> label. Likely same.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is that after tapping \"Select All\", the menu closes, and if you reopen it, the toggle shows \"Deselect All\", but tapping it *selects all again*? We tested it deselects. Good.\n\nI'm beginning to think the multi-file change is fine, and the seeded bug might be elsewhere.\n\nLet's think about the properties async task more concretely. Maybe the intended correct behavior: When the dialog opens, the size and date initially show placeholder (e.g., \"Calculating...\") then update once computed. The seeded bug might be that it never updates for *large* folders (duration). We only tested small folders. For a large folder like root's Android (3 items, 0 B) or Amaze (small), the computation is fast. We need a folder with a *large* tree to see if the background task actually completes. The device has huge app data under /storage/emulated/0/Android/data? We can't access com.amaze.filemanager contents due SAF but other apps' data may be accessible? Actually the \"data\" folder may contain several app dirs; com.amaze.filemanager was the only one? It showed 1 folder only. The Media folder may have many files. Let's inspect /storage/emulated/0/Android/media. We saw \"media\" folder earlier. It might contain app media files (e.g., WhatsApp). Let's check contents/size. This could be a large tree.\n\nLet's navigate to Android/media and check. Current root. Tap Android (11) -> media."}
