age volume's display name is stored as \"0\" because the code uses `storage.getID()` or something. Let's compare with the drawer's label \"Internal Storage\". The dialog's Name should match the drawer's display name \"Internal Storage\". It doesn't. That's a clear inconsistency: the storage volume properties dialog shows Name \"0\" and Location \"/storage/emulated\" whereas the volume is \"Internal Storage\" at /storage/emulated/0.\n\nAlso the \"Size\" shows 369 GB which equals the *free* space from the drawer (\"369 GB free of 452 GB\"), not the volume's total size (452 GB) or used size. If the property dialog \"Size\" is supposed to be total size, it's wrong. The date \"Nov 14 6:56 AM\" could be mount time.\n\nIs this dialog part of \"file details and properties\" as well? We accessed via drawer storage row's graph icon, so navigation drawer storage list. This is likely an area to test! The graph icon is part of the storage list. And the Name \"0\" is clearly a bug.\n\nBut wait: the drawer storage row showed \"Internal Storage\" but the properties Name \"0\" — maybe the \"Name\" is actually the *volume ID*? A user would expect \"Internal Storage\". This is a wrong value.\n\nBefore reporting, let's see if this is reproducible and if the values make sense. Also, what does the volume properties dialog normally look like in Amaze? It might show \"Name: Internal Storage\", \"Location: /storage/emulated/0\", \"Size: 452 GB\" etc. Our values look off.\n\nLet's check the dialog's screenshot to ensure."}
