{"type": "thinking", "text": "Correctly \"Deselect All\" when manually selecting all. Toggle is state-based. No bug.\n\nMaybe the seeded multi-file bug is about the *icon* or order? No.\n\nLet's test the toggle in an *empty* file list? Can't enter action mode with no items.\n\nMaybe the seeded multi-file bug is that after tapping \"Deselect All\", the last selected item remains selected visually? We saw clean.\n\nMaybe the bug is duplicate entries in the selection action bar? No.\n\nHmm. Maybe the multi-file overflow bug is about **\"Select All\" being an on/off toggle** but the menu title is *inverted*: when not all selected, it should say \"Select All\" (we see) and when all selected \"Deselect All\" (we see). Fine.\n\nCould be the bug for the *landscape toolbar*: when all selected, the toolbar button shows \"Deselect All\" and tapping it exits. Fine.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug isn't in the toggle action but in the menu *item presence*: For a single selection, the overflow includes \"Select All\"; when multiple, the overflow drops \"Share\"/\"Open with\"/\"Add Shortcut\" — that's normal.\n\nLet's move on. Maybe the seeded multi-file bug is in *bulk file operations*, e.g., when copying multiple files the count snackbar shows \"Copy: 0 folders and 2 files\" (correct), paste copies them (correct), delete dialog lists them (correct). We tested. Perhaps cutting multiple files: after cut, the source files remain until paste, and pasting should move and remove from source. Could be a bug: cut+paste copies but doesn't delete originals. That's a common multi-file bug! Let's test with two files into Alpha, then verify originals removed, then restore by moving back (or copy back). This changes data but can be reversed.\n\nTest procedure:\n1. In Amaze, select notes.txt + report+final.txt; tap Cut (not Copy).\n2. Go to Alpha; paste.\n3. Expected: both files appear in Alpha and are removed from Amaze (Amaze should show 2 folders and 2 files: keep.jpg, photo.jpg).\n4. Then move them back: select both in Alpha, Cut, go to Amaze, paste. Verify original state (4 files).\nThis is a good test of multi-file working and reversal. We have tested Copy/Delete; Cut is remaining.\n\nWe currently have all 6 selected with the overflow menu open (Deselect All). Let's close menu (BACK) and reset selection, then navigate to Amaze? Wait we're already in Amaze with all 6 selected. We can just tap Cut in the action bar (element 30) but that would cut all 6 (folders too) — we want only 2 files. Let's deselect all (tap 0 in menu = Deselect All) then select notes+report. Or press Done (26) then long-press notes and tap report. Let's do: tap Deselect All (0) to reset, then long-press notes (17) and tap report (23), then Cut (30). Let's do."}
